 "notes": [
  {
   "id": "vn-caro-recapture-toward-the-centre-doubled-is-fine",
   "line": "e4 c6 d4 d5 Nc3 dxe4 Nxe4 Nf6 Nxf6+ exf6",
   "teaches": "When you recapture, taking toward the centre usually beats taking toward the edge, even at the cost of doubled pawns. Doubled pawns that open a file for your pieces and build a wall in front of your king are a feature, not a flaw, and the file and the shelter are worth more than the tidy structure you gave up. Judge a pawn weakness by what it actually does, not by the name it carries.",
   "explains": "Capturing toward the centre doubles the f-pawns but opens the e-file that the rook will use once the king castles, and it leaves a solid block on f6, f7, g7 and h7 to shield the king. The structure looks damaged and is genuinely comfortable to play.",
